Installing
----------
Optional: Create a dir (Filelister) in Pfiles:

Copy Filelister.rexx, FilelisterCfg.rexx and FLcfg to PFiles:Filelister
or another directory - it does not matter, MCFilelister will automaticly
find the path.

Copy rexxsupport.library and rexxreqtools.library to libs:

Add the following line to bbsmenu - 1; Maintenance menu

FLC | {#0 pfiles:filelister/filelistercfg.rexx}
      |
     Ctrl-Q

Add the following line to bbsmenu - 2; Available everywhere

FL  | {#0 pfiles:filelister/filelister.rexx U}
      |
     Ctrl-Q

Reload the bbsmenu

If you want the filelister to run as an event add it as an arexx event with
the following argument:

pfiles:filelister/filelister.rexx


How to use
----------
 Filelister Config
 -----------------

NOTICE: The FilelisterConfig module ONLY works in LOCAL mode, that means
        you cannot run it from remote!

When you start the config-module you will be taken into the eventlist-
creator screen. It's a screen divided into two sections. The upper-sections
shows 4 of the configured event-lists.

The lists configured here will only be made if you run the filelister as an
event.

Pressing 'G' takes you to the user-config screen (the settings for the user-
created list).
- 'A' let you add a new filelist
- 'D' deletes the actual filelist
- 'E' edits the actual filelist
- 'Q' saves the configuration and quit
- cursorkeys select the actual filelist

Following is a description of the input-fields:

Filename:           Name for filelist WITHOUT .txt, .guide etc.
Description:        Description for this filelist
Type:               Text/Guide/HTML/HTML with frames - Type of filelist
Sort by:            Name/Date - Filelist sort by
Show upload area:   Yes/No - If no only areas with download access will be
                    shown, if yes also areas with upload or download access
                    will be shown
Show inv. only:     Yes/No - If no: Areas with invitation only flag not set
                    will not be shown - if yes the areas will be shown
Show private files: Yes/No - If no: Private files will not be shown - if yes:
                    private files will be shown.
Fileflags:          Fileflag for this filelist (as user-flags), currently you
                    must specify it as a number!! - that means if you select
                    flag 2, you must specify '4' which is the decimal value of
                    fileflag 2 - to calculate the value you must calculate to
                    value for each flag and the add them. To calculate a flag
                    you say flag^2.
Min. accesslevel:   Minimum accesslevel needed to get into list
Number of days:     Maximum age of files in list (0 = No maximum)
Filepath:           Path for filelists
Header file:        Filelist header - if none selected no header in filelist 
Footer file:        Filelist footer - if none selected no footer in filelist 

On the global configuration screen there are following input-fileds

Temp.directory:     The path for temporary files
Description:        Description for user-created files - the type of list will
                    be added to the description (eg. full filelist, 7 days
                    back)
Show upload area:   Yes/No - If no only areas with download access will be
                    shown, if yes also areas with upload or download access
                    will be shown
Show inv. only:     Yes/No - If no: Areas with invitation only flag not set
                    will not be shown - if yes the areas will be shown
Show private files: Yes/No - If no: Private files will not be shown - if yes:
                    private files will be shown.
Header file:        Filelist header - if none selected no header in filelist 
Footer file:        Filelist footer - if none selected no footer in filelist 

When EDITING entrys you select the entry with cursorkeys and then press ENTER.

The rest of the system should be self-explaining - else write a note to me
so I can add it to the documentation.


